From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bogdan <189150777+bogdan-od@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] Make SSE floating-point NaN results independent of the
 host CPU

wasm leaves the sign and payload of a NaN produced by a float operation to the
host: x86 gives ffc00000, ARM gives 7fc00000. The xmm registers end up in the
memory checksum of a recorded session, so a recording made on one machine did
not replay on another.

Route every arithmetic SSE/SSE2 operation (add, sub, mul, div, sqrt, rsqrt,
rcp, min, max, conversions between f32 and f64) through small non-inlined
helpers that build a NaN result from the operand bits by the x86 rule: the
first NaN operand with the quiet bit set, otherwise the "indefinite" value.
